content.thinking:
Alright, I’ve just finished a series of CSS enhancements: added the motion keyframes (rise, glow‑drift, grid‑drift, line‑draw), applied reveal animations to the hero text, gave the person cards a smoother hover transition, and even animated the background grid. The next logical step is to bring the remaining visual elements into the same animated flow.

Looking through the current stylesheet (slm_alliance.html), I see a simple .accent-line rule defined as:

```
.accent-line {
    width: 50px;
    height: 2px;
    background: #a8926a;
    margin: 1rem auto 1.5rem;
}
```

This line is used as a decorative separator in several sections. Since I already have a `line-draw` keyframe (which scales an element from 0 to 1 on the X‑axis), I can make the accent line animate on entry just like the other “reveal” elements. To do that, the line needs a defined transform origin (center) so the scaling works correctly, and I need to attach an animation when the element receives the `.in` class (or when its parent has `.reveal.in`). The pattern for other elements is:

```
.reveal.in .some-element,
.some-element.in {
    animation: <keyframe> <duration> <timing> <delay> backwards;
}
```

So I’ll add a block for `.accent-line` that follows this pattern, using `line-draw` with a short 0.8s duration, the same cubic‑bezier timing I used elsewhere, and a slight delay of 0.2s to stagger it nicely.

Next, I notice there’s a “mission‑goal” component elsewhere in the markup that currently has no hover styling. To keep the UI consistent, I should give it a subtle transition on border‑color and box‑shadow, and on hover change the border color to a lighter shade of the accent color and add a soft glow. This mirrors the hover effect I already added for `.person-card`.

Both of these changes can be made by editing the existing `.accent-line` block (adding `transform-origin`) and then appending the new CSS rules right after it. Since the old block is a unique exact match, I’ll use a non‑replace‑all edit targeting that string and replace it with the expanded version that includes the new rules and the additional `.mission-goal` sections.

Thus, the edit parameters should be:
- `file_path`: "/home/lane/MythosMini/slm_alliance.html"
- `old_string`: the exact current `.accent-line` block
- `new_string`: the same block plus `transform-origin: center;`, followed by the new `.reveal.in .accent-line, .accent-line.in` animation block, and the `.mission-goal` transition/hover block.

Executing this edit will integrate the accent line into the reveal animation flow and give the mission‑goal cards a polished hover effect, completing the visual polish I’ve been building up.

arguments.new_string:
.accent-line {
    width: 50px;
    height: 2px;
    background: #a8926a;
    margin: 1rem auto 1.5rem;
    transform-origin: center;
}

.reveal.in .accent-line,
.accent-line.in {
    animation: line-draw 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) 0.2s backwards;
}

.mission-goal {
    transition: border-color 0.35s ease, box-shadow 0.35s ease;
}

.mission-goal:hover {
    border-color: #a8926a66;
    box-shadow: 0 0 24px -8px #a8926a33;
}
